WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.443
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:05.743 --> 00:00:09.118
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:17.446
Unit sixteen: Reading Comprehension: Multiple Choice and True/False. Today you will read a text and answer questions accurately.

4
00:00:17.746 --> 00:00:20.305
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.871
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:26.880
Comprehension.

7
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:30.603
Comprehension means understanding what you read.

8
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.112
Reading comprehension is important.

9
00:00:33.717 --> 00:00:36.299
Your turn. Say: Comprehension.

10
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:40.123
Comprehension.

11
00:00:40.883 --> 00:00:41.652
Skim.

12
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.625
Skim means to read quickly for the general idea.

13
00:00:46.217 --> 00:00:47.798
Skim the text first.

14
00:00:48.383 --> 00:00:50.664
Your turn. Say: Skim.

15
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.571
Skim.

16
00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:56.144
Scan.

17
00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.649
Scan means to look for a specific detail.

18
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.948
Scan for a name or number.

19
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.423
Your turn. Say: Scan.

20
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.152
Scan.

21
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:10.442
True.

22
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.264
True means agreeing with the text.

23
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.223
The statement is true.

24
00:01:15.817 --> 00:01:18.156
Your turn. Say: True.

25
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:21.769
True.

26
00:01:22.517 --> 00:01:23.425
False.

27
00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.706
False means the opposite of the text.

28
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:28.794
The statement is false.

29
00:01:29.383 --> 00:01:31.815
Your turn. Say: False.

30
00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:35.424
False.

31
00:01:36.183 --> 00:01:37.184
Evidence.

32
00:01:38.183 --> 00:01:40.903
Evidence means facts that prove an answer.

33
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:43.365
Find evidence in the text.

34
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.776
Your turn. Say: Evidence.

35
00:01:49.633 --> 00:01:50.727
Evidence.

36
00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:52.345
Detail.

37
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:56.023
Detail means a small piece of information.

38
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:57.769
Find the detail.

39
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:00.525
Your turn. Say: Detail.

40
00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.286
Detail.

41
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.330
Main idea.

42
00:02:07.317 --> 00:02:09.479
Main idea means the central point.

43
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:11.607
What is the main idea?

44
00:02:12.217 --> 00:02:15.519
Your turn. Say: Main idea.

45
00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:19.646
Main idea.

46
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:23.805
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.462
Visal, how should I read a passage in the exam?

48
00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:39.030
First skim the passage for the main idea. Then read each question and scan the text for the answer. Read the sentences around your keyword before you choose.

49
00:02:40.117 --> 00:02:42.418
How do I answer true or false questions?

50
00:02:43.517 --> 00:02:53.547
Find the sentence in the text. If it agrees with the statement, choose true. If it says the opposite, choose false. Do not use your own knowledge.

51
00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.359
What mistakes should I avoid?

52
00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:07.126
Do not choose an option only because it uses the same words as the text. Check the meaning, and cross out options you know are wrong before you decide.

53
00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.709
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.744
Grammar focus: Strategy: skim, scan, check evidence.

55
00:03:15.044 --> 00:03:16.219
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:19.357
Skim the text to find the main idea.

57
00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.389
Scan for a name, a date or a number.

58
00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:30.154
Skim first, then scan for each answer. Choose true or false only from the text and check the evidence before you decide.

59
00:03:30.917 --> 00:03:34.753
Be careful! Don't say: I use my own knowledge for the answer.

60
00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.280
Say: I find the answer in the text.

61
00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.231
Evidence from the text.

62
00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:44.871
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.016
A Short Passage.

64
00:03:47.316 --> 00:03:50.326
Rathana reads a passage about the Tonle Sap Lake.

65
00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:54.285
It says the lake grows much larger in the rainy season.

66
00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.135
Many families catch fish there and live on boats.

67
00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:02.120
A statement says the lake is the same size all year.

68
00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:06.120
That statement is false because the text says the opposite.

69
00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:11.897
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.564
Skimming is for finding blank.

71
00:04:14.864 --> 00:04:18.540
A, a spelling. B, the main idea. C, a number.

72
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.634
The answer is B: the main idea.

73
00:04:25.783 --> 00:04:28.305
If the text says the opposite, choose blank.

74
00:04:28.605 --> 00:04:32.166
A, true. B, not sure. C, false.

75
00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.560
The answer is C: false.

76
00:04:38.717 --> 00:04:41.088
What happens to the lake in the rainy season?

77
00:04:41.388 --> 00:04:46.330
A, it grows larger. B, it disappears. C, it freezes.

78
00:04:49.867 --> 00:04:52.458
The answer is A: it grows larger.

79
00:04:53.617 --> 00:04:55.372
You should not use blank.

80
00:04:55.672 --> 00:04:59.395
A, keywords. B, your own knowledge. C, the text.

81
00:05:02.933 --> 00:05:05.339
The answer is B: your own knowledge.

82
00:05:06.483 --> 00:05:08.367
Many families live on blank.

83
00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:12.042
A, mountains. B, trains. C, boats.

84
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.774
The answer is C: boats.

85
00:05:18.967 --> 00:05:22.269
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:23.117 --> 00:05:25.209
How do you answer reading questions?

87
00:05:34.017 --> 00:05:35.517
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:35.817 --> 00:05:48.712
I skim the passage for the main idea and then read each question carefully. I scan for keywords and read the sentences around them. I choose the answer that is supported by the text.

89
00:05:49.012 --> 00:05:50.698
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:57.219
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: skim, scan, check evidence.

91
00:05:57.519 --> 00:06:02.471
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

92
00:06:02.771 --> 00:06:05.516
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:05.816 --> 00:06:08.364
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

